  "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of rolls in which the die landed on an odd number to the total number of rolls is $\\frac{5}{8}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of rolls resulting in an odd number, and the denominator represents the total number of rolls.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $40$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 5}{8\\times 5}=\\frac{25}{40}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the die landed on an odd number $25$ times.\nSo, the number of times the die landed on an even number is\n\n$$\n40-25=15.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
